{"availability":"available","full":"firecrawl/anydoc","name":"anydoc","description":"Convert Word, PowerPoint, Excel, OpenDocument, RTF, EPUB, CSV, and PDF to clean Markdown. Built in Rust, with Node.js and Python bindings.","category":"Productivity","language":"Rust","stars":22858,"forks":1470,"created":"2026-08-03T16:36:14Z","updated":"2026-08-28T02:13:16Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://firecrawl.github.io/anydoc/","topics":[],"demo":"https://firecrawl.github.io/anydoc/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:00.012Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:00.012Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:00.012Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T04:29:16.030Z","stars":22698,"forks":1440},{"at":"2026-10-15T13:02:00.012Z","stars":22858,"forks":1470}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Fast Rust library that converts documents (Word, PowerPoint, Excel, OpenDocument, RTF, EPUB, CSV, and PDF) into clean GitHub-Flavored Markdown. Includes bindings for Node.js, Python, and the browser (WebAssembly).","Built by Firecrawl to turn any office document into LLM-ready Markdown in single-digit milliseconds, with one consistent output no matter which format goes in. It powers Firecrawl Parse, so if you'd rather not run it yourself, the hosted API gives you the same conversion plus our OCR models for the scanned pages anydoc can't read on its own.","Try it in your browser: the demo page runs the library as WebAssembly, so files are converted locally and never leave your machine."],"features":["One output for every format. Each format parses into a shared document model and renders through a single Markdown serializer, so escaping, tables, heading anchors, and footnotes behave identically whether the input was…","Full document structure. Headings with anchors, bold/italic/strikethrough, inline code and code blocks, links and internal cross-references, bulleted/numbered/nested/task lists with the source's own numbering, tables…","Equations as LaTeX. Word and PowerPoint (OMML), OpenDocument and EPUB (MathML), and RTF equations convert to GitHub-flavored math: $...$ inline and $$ blocks.","Embedded assets. Images and embedded objects render as their alt text in the Markdown, and the raw bytes stay available on the document model, tagged with their media type. Images with an external URL become ordinary…","Content-based format detection. The format is read from the bytes themselves (PDF header, RTF open group, OLE stream names, ZIP package mimetype), so mislabeled files still convert correctly."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/firecrawl/anydoc/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0cc4383125c1640584f73b4630499529c9a7188b97c17d82065f9a9dad5b7cb6","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:16.158Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:00.161Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Fast Rust library that converts documents (Word, PowerPoint, Excel, OpenDocument, RTF, EPUB, CSV, and PDF) into clean GitHub-Flavored Markdown. Includes bindings for Node.js, Python, and the browser (WebAssembly).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/firecrawl/anydoc/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"0cc4383125c1640584f73b4630499529c9a7188b97c17d82065f9a9dad5b7cb6","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/firecrawl/anydoc/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:00.161Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-28T02:13:16Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/firecrawl/anydoc/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T13:02:00.162Z","hash":"0cc4383125c1640584f73b4630499529c9a7188b97c17d82065f9a9dad5b7cb6","originalBytes":16795,"storedBytes":16795,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["format","markdown","anydoc","document","bytes","python","firecrawl","ocr","node","csv","readme.md","api","hosted","one","pdf","which","agent","formats","rtf","content","documents","file","model","npm","pages","rust","wasm","anydoc.to","bash",